          {
            "raw_output": "downstream_apps/sf_triggers/lightning_modules/:\n__init__.py\npl_simple_baseline.py\n=== builders build_datasets ===\n110:def build_helio_dataloaders(\n111-    cfg,\n112-    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n113-    scalers: Any = None,\n114-    num_workers: int | None = None,\n115-    seed: int | None = None,\n116-    **task_kwargs,\n117-) -> Tuple[DataLoader, DataLoader]:\n118-    \"\"\"Build the train and validation DataLoaders described by ``cfg``.\n119-\n120-    Args:\n121-        cfg: A ``TrainingConfig`` from ``load_config()``.\n122-        dataset_cls: ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` or a subclass of it.\n123-        scalers: Normalization statistics; built from the config if omitted.\n124-        num_workers: Override for ``cfg.num_workers`` (useful in notebooks, where fewer\n125-            workers start faster).\n126-        seed: Seed for the shuffle order and the per-worker RNGs. Defaults to ``cfg.seed``.\n127-            Pinning it explicitly is what makes the epoch order depend only on the config:\n128-            a bare ``shuffle=True`` seeds its sampler from whatever the global torch RNG\n129-            state happens to be when the iterator is created, so anything that consumes\n130-            RNG earlier in the program silently reshuffles the data.\n131-        **task_kwargs: Extra keyword arguments forwarded to ``dataset_cls``.\n132-\n133-    Returns:\n134-        ``(train_loader, val_loader)``. Only the training loader shuffles.\n135-    \"\"\"\n136-    train_dataset, val_dataset = build_helio_datasets(\n137-        cfg, dataset_cls, scalers=scalers, **task_kwargs\n138-    )\n139-\n140-    workers = cfg.num_workers if num_workers is None else num_workers\n141-    base_seed = cfg.seed if seed is None else seed\n142-\n143-    loader_kwargs = dict(\n144-        batch_size=cfg.batch_size,\n145-        num_workers=workers,\n146-        pin_memory=True,\n147-        drop_last=True,\n148-    )\n149-    if workers > 0:\n150-        # \"spawn\": the dataset holds an s3fs/boto3 handle that does not survive fork.\n151-        # Both of these are rejected outright when num_workers == 0.\n152-        loader_kwargs[\"multiprocessing_context\"] = \"spawn\"\n153-        loader_kwargs[\"persistent_workers\"] = True\n154-        loader_kwargs[\"worker_init_fn\"] = partial(_seed_worker, base_seed=base_seed)\n155-\n156-    # An explicit generator makes the shuffle a function of the seed alone, rather than\n157-    # of the global RNG state at the moment the iterator happens to be created.\n158-    shuffle_generator = torch.Generator()\n159-    shuffle_generator.manual_seed(base_seed)\n160-\n161-    train_loader = DataLoader(\n162-        train_dataset, shuffle=True, generator=shuffle_generator, **loader_kwargs\n163-    )\n164-    # No generator for validation: it is not shuffled, so there is nothing to seed.\n165-    val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, shuffle=False, **loader_kwargs)\n166-    return train_loader, val_loader\nShell cwd was reset to /home/jovyan/adi_wdir/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/sf_triggers",
